nimport { unstable_cache } from \"next/cache\";\n\nexport const listSources = unstable_cache(\n  async () => {\n    const rows = await getDb().select().from(sources).orderBy(sources.createdAt);\n    return rows.map((row) => sourceSchema.parse(row));\n  },\n  [\"sources-list\"],\n  { tags: [\"sources\"] },\n);\n```\nPair with `revalidateTag(\"sources\")` on any future create/update mutation. At minimum, wrap with React's `cache()` so multiple calls within one request tree dedupe automatically.\n\n### 4. Memory leaks\nNothing to report — no `useEffect`, `addEventListener`, `setInterval`/`setTimeout`, or subscriptions exist anywhere in the repo.\n\n### 5. Redundant computations\nNothing to report — no expensive per-render filtering/sorting/parsing found.\n\n---\n\n**Recommendation:** the codebase is pre-scale, so there's little to optimize yet. The one real fix is deduping `listSources`/`countSourcesBySide` and adding caching to `lib/server/sources.ts`. The bigger thing to get ahead of: when you build list/detail pages for `runs`, `entities`, `matches`, and `conflicts`, use Drizzle relational queries (`with:`) from the start — that's exactly the shape where N+1 patterns creep in later.\n",
